# Class: obo:FOODON_00001138 (tea based beverage product)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00001138 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00001138 "A beverage product derived from leaves of the tea plant (Camellia sinensis)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_00001138 wikipedia:Tea)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:FOODON_00001138 "Damion Dooley"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_00001138 "\"While fermentation is also referred to in the production of brewed teas, this is inaccurate. Some herbal teas on the market today include probiotic cultures alongside tea leaves to maintain gut health but the tea itself hasn't been fermented. Most dried teas however don't use live cultures at all during production. Instead, harvested tea leaves undergo a natural chemical process known as oxidation, which also changes the color, flavor and level of health benefits in the resulting brew.\" [https://eatcultured.com/blogs/our-awesome-blog/fermented-tea]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00001138 "tea based beverage product"@en)
EquivalentClasses(obo:FOODON_00001138 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:FOODON_00002275 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001000 obo:NCBITaxon_4442)))
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00001138 obo:FOODON_00001255)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00001138 obo:FOODON_00002275)

