# Class: obo:FOODON_00001154 (citrullus lanatus fruit food product)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00001154 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00001154 "Citrullus lanatus is a plant species in the family Cucurbitaceae, a vine-like (scrambler and trailer) flowering plant originally from sub-Saharan Africa. It is cultivated for its fruit. The subdivision of this species into two varieties, watermelons (Citrullus lanatus (Thunb.) var. lanatus) and citron melons (Citrullus lanatus var. citroides (L. H. Bailey) Mansf.)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:FOODON_00001154 "Damion Dooley"@en)
