AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000119 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Areca_nut"^^xsd:anyURI) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00001642 "The areca nut (/ˈærɪkə/ or /əˈriːkə/) is the fruit of the areca palm (Areca catechu), which grows in much of the tropical Pacific (Melanesia and Micronesia), Southeast and South Asia, and parts of east Africa. This fruit is commonly referred to as betel nut so it is easily confused with betel (Piper betle) leaves that are often used to wrap it (paan)."@en)
