# Class: obo:FOODON_00001993 (langostino food product)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00001993 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00001993 "A langostino food product is a food product encompassing a variety of species of prawn, crayfish or spot lobster depending on which speech community is involking it."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_00001993 wikipedia:Langostino)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000600 obo:FOODON_00001993 "In the United States, the Food and Drug Administration allows \"langostino\" to be used as a market name for three species of squat lobster in the family Galatheidae: Cervimunida johni, Munida gregaria, and Pleuroncodes monodon. In Spain, it means some species of prawns. In Cuba and other Spanish-speaking Caribbean islands, the name langostino is also used to refer to crayfish. In Argentina the name is used to refer to Pleoticus muelleri, a kind of shrimp, while in Chile and Peru it refers to Pleuroncodes monodon. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Langostino]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:FOODON_00001993 "Damion Dooley"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:date obo:FOODON_00001993 "2020-01-24T16:30:06Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00001993 "langostino food product"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00001993 obo:FOODON_00001792)

