# Class: obo:FOODON_00002477 (game animal food product)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_00002477 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00002477 "Game or quarry is any animal hunted for sport or for food. The type and range of animals hunted for food varies in different parts of the world. In some countries, game is classified, including legal classification with respect to licences required, as either \"small game\" or \"large game\""@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_00002477 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_(hunting)"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:FOODON_00002477 "Damion Dooley"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_00002477 "\"Typically, it falls into two categories: ‘feathered’ or ‘furred’. Feathered game or game birds include grouse, pheasant, partridge, quail, snipe, wild duck, woodcock and wood pigeon. Furred game includes hare, rabbit, venison and ‘wild’ boar.\" [source: http://welshgamemeat.wales/en/what-is-game-meat/]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00002477 "game animal food product"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_00002477 obo:FOODON_00001092)

