AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000600 obo:FOODON_03307094 "Despite the name \"plum pudding\", the pudding contains no actual plums due to the pre-Victorian use of the word \"plums\" as a term for raisins. The pudding is traditionally composed of thirteen ingredients, symbolizing Jesus and the Twelve Apostles, including many dried fruits held together by egg and suet, sometimes moistened by treacle or molasses and flavoured with cinnamon, nutmeg, cloves, ginger, and other spices. The pudding is usually aged for a month or more, or even a year; the high alcohol content of the pudding prevents it from spoiling during this time.[wikipedia:Christmas_pudding]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03307094 siren:F7094)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03307094 "plum pudding"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03307094 "SIREN DB annotation:
* whole, shape achieved by forming FOODON:03430147
* fully heat-treated FOODON:03440014
* fruit, peel present, core, pit or seed present FOODON:03420140
* alcoholated FOODON:03460160
* ingredient: spice or herb added FOODON:03460151
* ingredient: grain added FOODON:03460152
* ingredient: animal fat or oil added FOODON:03460262"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03307094 "Christmas pudding"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03307094 obo:FOODON_00003290)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03307094 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:FOODON_00002420 obo:FOODON_03311488))
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03307094 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002350 obo:FOODON_03400222))

