AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03316078 "Soda bread is a variety of quick bread traditionally made in a variety of cuisines in which sodium bicarbonate (otherwise known as \"baking soda\", or in Ireland, \"bread soda\") is used as a leavening agent instead of the traditional yeast. The ingredients of traditional soda bread are flour, baking soda, salt, and buttermilk."@en)
