# Class: obo:FOODON_03316764 (vanilla bean extract)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03316764 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03316764 "Vanilla extract is a solution containing the flavor compound vanillin as the primary ingredient.  It is made by macerating and percolating vanilla pods in a solution of ethanol and water."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03316764 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla"^^xsd:anyURI)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:FOODON_03316764 "vanilla"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03316764 "natural vanilla"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03316764 "Wikipedia notes: Pure vanilla extract is made by macerating and percolating vanilla pods in a solution of ethanol and water. 

In the United States, in order for a vanilla extract to be called pure, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration requires that the solution contains a minimum of 35% alcohol and 100 g of vanilla beans per litre (13.35 ounces per gallon).

Canadian Regulations: Under the Food and Drug Regulations (C.R.C., c. 870), vanilla extract products have to be processed from vanilla beans: Vanilla planifolia or Vanilla tahitensia."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03316764 "vanilla bean extract"@en)
EquivalentClasses(obo:FOODON_03316764 ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 ObjectUnionOf(obo:CHEBI_18346 obo:CHEBI_48408)) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002353 obo:FOODON_00002414)))
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03316764 obo:FOODON_00002328)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03316764 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:FOODON_00001301 obo:FOODON_00002396))

